Subject: [PATCH] vulkan: leave unbound acceleration structure slots unwritten without nullDescriptor

A program layout can hold acceleration structure slots that the bound pipeline's
shaders never use (module-scope parameters of other entry points). Without the
nullDescriptor feature (MoltenVK) slang-rhi asserted while writing a null descriptor
there; release builds already skipped the write. Vulkan only requires valid
descriptors for statically used bindings, so skipping the write is correct in every
build. Upstreamable.

---
--- a/src/vulkan/vk-shader-object.cpp
+++ b/src/vulkan/vk-shader-object.cpp
@@ -112,12 +112,11 @@
 )
 {
     // The Vulkan spec states: If the nullDescriptor feature is not enabled, each element of
-    // pAccelerationStructures must not be VK_NULL_HANDLE
+    // pAccelerationStructures must not be VK_NULL_HANDLE. Leave the slot unwritten instead:
+    // that is valid for bindings the pipeline's shaders never use, such as the module-scope
+    // acceleration structure of another entry point in the same program layout.
     if (!as && !device->m_api.m_extendedFeatures.robustness2Features.nullDescriptor)
-    {
-        SLANG_RHI_ASSERT_FAILURE("nullDescriptor feature is not available on the device");
         return;
-    }
 
     VkWriteDescriptorSetAccelerationStructureKHR writeAS = {};
     writeAS.sType = VK_STRUCTURE_TYPE_WRITE_DESCRIPTOR_SET_ACCELERATION_STRUCTURE_KHR;
